※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ `→ T in a` says the answer was made in the arena parameter `a` names, or in something that
※ lasts at least as long -- `⎕heap`, a literal, a variable at the top level.  A caller then
※ knows the answer lives as long as what it handed to `a`, and may give back every other arena
※ it handed over and keep the answer.  Without it a caller can only take the answer to be made
※ in any arena it handed over, which never lets freed memory be read but refuses programs like
※ this one.
※
※ `→ T in a, b` says it may be either, so it lives as long as the shorter.  `s: T in a` says a
※ parameter was made in what `a` names, which is what lets a body answer it under `in a`.
※
※ Compare: **Rust** with an arena crate, `fn label<'b>(a: &'b Bump) -> &'b str`, which is this
※ with the lifetime written out; **Cyclone**'s regions, `char *ρ label(region_t<ρ> r)`.

let std := ⎕import("std")

※ Working space in one arena, the answer in the other.  The join copies the bytes, so the
※ answer is made in `a` and nothing of `b` is in it.
fn label(a: &mut arena, b: &mut arena, v: u16) → str in a:
    let scratch: str = ⍕v in b
    "#" ⧺ scratch in a

※ A parameter made in the arena the answer is made in may be the answer.
fn either(c: bool, a: &mut arena, s: str in a) → str in a:
    if c: s else: "-" ⧺ s in a

※ Either of two, so what the caller gets lasts as long as the shorter.
fn one_of(c: bool, a: &mut arena, b: &mut arena) → str in a, b:
    if c: "x" ⧺ "y" in a else: "z" ⧺ "w" in b

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let long: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(long)
    let short: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let name: str = label(&mut long, &mut short, 7u16)
    ⎕empty(short)
    if name ≠ "#7":
        return 1u6
    ※ `std.text` says it too: its answer outlives an arena it was not made in.
    let said: str = std.text(42u16, &mut long)
    ⎕empty(short)
    if said ≠ "42":
        return 2u6
    let held: str = "ab" ⧺ "c" in long
    if either(false, &mut long, held) ≠ "-abc":
        return 3u6
    ※ Text from ⎕heap lasts longer than any arena, so it may stand for one made in `a`.
    if either(true, &mut long, "lit") ≠ "lit":
        return 4u6
    let both: str = one_of(true, &mut long, &mut short)
    if both ≠ "xy":
        return 5u6
    0u6
